1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.
我是你的中国旅游专家

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,100
This kind of town survived 800 years — with no walls.
这样的古城·活了800年·却没城墙

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,500
Most old Chinese cities were ringed in stone.
中国古城·多有石墙环绕

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Here the ruling chieftains chose to leave it open.
这里的土司·偏不设墙

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,500
One tale: their surname meant "Wood" — a frame would trap it.
传说姓"木"·加框成"困"

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Snowmelt runs through every lane in stone canals.
雪水入渠·穿巷而过

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,500
One well, three pools: drink, wash food, wash clothes.
一井三眼·饮·洗菜·洗衣

8
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,000
Over 300 old bridges cross the streams.
三百多座古桥·跨水而立

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,400
The Naxi still write in living pictographs.
纳西东巴文·活着的象形字

10
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,200
★ Expert Tip: Wander before 8am — the lanes are yours before the tour flags.
★8点前来·旅行团未到最静

11
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,800
A town with no walls, alive 800 years — would you wander in?
无墙古城·活了800年·你想走进吗？
